  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Rajesh Kumar vs The State Of Madhya Pradesh on 22 September, 2017 1 High Court Of Madhya Pradesh, Principal Seat At Jabalpur (Single Bench : Hon'Ble Shri Justice J.P.Gupta) M.Cr.C.No. 2722/ 2006 Rajesh Kumar and two others Vs. State of Madhya Pradesh Shri Surendra Singh, learned Senior Advocate with Shri Ashwani Dubey, Advocate for the petitioners. Shri R. N. Yadav, Panel Lawyer for the respondents-State.",
    "facts": "Apart form it, the petitioners no. 2 and 3 were failed to pro- duce license for selling of food articles which is also violation of Rule 50 of the Prevention of Food Adulteration Rules, 1955. 2. The aforesaid proceedings have been challenged mainly on the ground that the provisions of Rule 32 (i) of the Prevention of Food Adulteration Rules, 1955 was not in existence on 24.10.1997. Therefore, no question for violation of the Rules arises. Similarly, Rule 50 of the Food Adulteration Rules, 1955 is not applicable as the Jam is a food arti- cle which comes in purview of Food Products Order, 1955 and by provi- so to the said Rules such articles have been exempted. In such circum- stances, the proceeding of the prosecution of petitioner no. 1 as a Sell- er and petitioners no. 2 and 3 as the Directors of Manufacturer Compa- ny of the Product are bad in law and misuse of process of the court. Hence, the proceedings be [LEAKAGE_MASK].",
    "arguments": "3. Learned PL has opposed the aforesaid contentions and prayed for rejection of the petition.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "3. Learned PL has opposed the aforesaid contentions and prayed for rejection of the petition.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
